# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your Supabase dashboard.
#
# Quickest way to get both values: the "Connect" button at the top of the
# project dashboard. Otherwise they live in two separate places:
#   URL  ->  Settings -> Data API
#   Key  ->  Settings -> API Keys
#
# The URL is always https://<project-ref>.supabase.co, and <project-ref> is the
# id in your dashboard address bar.
#
# For the key, either of these works — both map to the same `anon` Postgres
# role, so Row Level Security treats them identically:
#   * a publishable key   sb_publishable_...   (current)
#   * a legacy anon key   eyJhbGci...          (older projects)
#
# NEVER put a secret key (sb_secret_... / service_role) here. Those bypass RLS
# completely, and anything in this file is compiled into the browser bundle.
# The Edge Function gets its own service-role key injected by the platform.
#
# Both values below are safe to expose: the anon/publishable key only ever
# grants what RLS allows, and every write is gated on public.is_admin().

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here
